	    <div class="fr-view">


        <h2 class="subhead1">2026 Election Dates<br><span style="font-size: 14px;"><span style="font-size: 14px;">General Election - November 3, 2026</span></span></h2><h2 id="isPasted">Early In-Person Absentee Voting&nbsp;</h2><p><span style="color: rgb(35, 31, 32); font-family: Poppins; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; display: inline !important; float: none;"><span style="color: rgb(35, 31, 32); font-family: Poppins; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; display: inline !important; float: none;" data-pasted="true">Early in-person absentee voting is located in Greenfield City Hall 7325 W. Forest Home Ave., Common Council Chambers, Room 100 during the following dates and times:</span></span><br><br>Tuesday, October 20, 2026, 8 AM &ndash; 5 PM<br>Wednesday, October 21, 2026, 8 AM &ndash; 6 PM<br>Thursday, October 22, 2026, 8 AM &ndash; 5 PM<br>Friday, October 23, 2026, 8 AM &ndash; 5 PM<br>Saturday, October 24, 2026, 10 AM &ndash; NOON<br>Monday, October 26, 2026, 8 AM &ndash; 5 PM<br>Tuesday, October 27, 2026, 8 AM &ndash; 5 PM<br>Wednesday, October 28, 2026, 8 AM &ndash; 6 PM<br>Thursday, October 29, 2026, 8 AM &ndash; 5 PM<br>Friday, October 30, 2026, 8 AM &ndash; 5 PM</p><h2 id="isPasted">Election Day Polling Locations</h2><p><span style="color: rgb(35, 31, 32); font-family: Poppins; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; display: inline !important; float: none;" data-pasted="true">Election Day polling locations are open from 7:00 AM until 8:00 PM on Election Day. A photo ID is required to vote. All polling places are accessible to elderly voters and voters with disabilities</span></p><table class="fr-alternate-rows" style="width: 100%;"><tbody><tr><td style="width: 18.3842%; text-align: left; vertical-align: middle;"><strong>Wards</strong></td><td style="width: 48.3412%; vertical-align: middle;"><strong>Facility Name</strong></td><td style="width: 33.3333%; vertical-align: bottom;"><strong>Address</strong></td></tr><tr><td style="width: 18.3842%;">1-12</td><td style="width: 48.3412%;">Greenfield Community Center</td><td style="width: 33.3333%;">7215 W Cold Spring Rd</td></tr><tr><td style="width: 18.3842%;">13-16</td><td style="width: 48.3412%;">The Ridge Community Church</td><td style="width: 33.3333%;">4500 S 108th St</td></tr><tr><td style="width: 18.3842%;">17-21</td><td style="width: 48.3412%;">Greenfield Public Library</td><td style="width: 33.3333%;">5310 W Layton Ave</td></tr><tr><td style="width: 18.3842%;">22-26</td><td style="width: 48.3412%;">Adoration Lutheran Church</td><td style="width: 33.3333%;">3840 W Edgerton Ave</td></tr></tbody></table><p><br><span id="isPasted">Find your polling location on&nbsp;</span><span id="isPasted"><a href="https://myvote.wi.gov/en-us/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MyVote WI</a></span><span id="isPasted">.</span></p><h2 id="isPasted">Sample Ballots-</h2><p id="isPasted">Find your sample ballot on <a href="https://myvote.wi.gov/en-us/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MyVote Wisconsin</a>. From the main page select &ldquo;What&rsquo;s On My Ballot?&rdquo;, enter your address, and search.&nbsp;</p><h2>Referendum Questions and Explanations-</h2><p><span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody" data-pasted="true"><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/13143" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Explanatory Statements for State Referendum Questions 1, 2 &amp; 3</a></span><br><span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody" data-pasted="true"><span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody" data-pasted="true"><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/13142" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Explanatory Statement for Greenfield School District Referendum, Question 1</a></span></span><span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody" data-pasted="true"><span data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody" data-pasted="true"><br data-pasted="true"></span></span><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/13144" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Explanatory Statement for Greenfield School District Referendum, Question 2</a></p><h2 id="isPasted">You may Return your Absentee Ballot by <span style="text-decoration: underline;">any</span> of the following ways-</h2><ul style="box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px 0px 1.4em; padding: 0px 0px 0px 3em; font-family: Poppins; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; color: rgb(35, 31, 32); line-height: 1.5; list-style-type: circle; font-size: 13.28px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;"><li style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-bottom: 0.35em; font-size: 14px;">Mail your ballot. Allow at least one week for mail.*&nbsp;</li><li style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-bottom: 0.35em; font-size: 14px;">Personally deliver your ballot to the City Clerk&rsquo;s office, Room 102.*&nbsp;<br>Please note that the clerk shall secure the ballot and cause the ballot to be delivered to the polling place serving the elector&rsquo;s residence before 8 PM on Election Day. Please also note that, if returning your ballot to the City Clerk&rsquo;s office <span style="text-decoration: underline;" data-pasted="true">on</span> Election Day, the ballot must be delivered by 7 PM in order to ensure its timely delivery to the polling place by the Clerk&rsquo;s Office by 8 PM. &nbsp;Any ballot not mailed or delivered as provided in this subsection may not be counted, Wis. Stat. 6.87 (6).</li><li style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-bottom: 0.35em; font-size: 14px;">Personally deliver your ballot to your polling location on Election Day, November 3, 2026, between the hours of 7 AM and 8 PM.*<br>The ballot shall be returned so it is delivered to the polling place no later than 8 PM on Election Day, Wis. Stat. 6.87(6).</li><li style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-bottom: 0.35em; font-size: 14px;">Personally deliver your ballot to the drop box, located in the wall on the south side of the Greenfield City Hall building, 7325 W. Forest Home Ave.*&nbsp;<br>The drop box closes at 7 PM on Election Day, November 3, 2026. After 7 PM, you may personally deliver your ballot to your polling location no later than 8 PM, or personally deliver your ballot to the City Clerk&rsquo;s office, Room 102, by 7 PM so your ballot may be delivered to the polling place serving the elector&rsquo;s residence before 8 PM, Wis. Stat. 6.87(6).</li></ul><p style="box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 1.4em; color: rgb(35, 31, 32); font-family: Poppins; font-size: 13.28px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-weight: inherit; font-style: inherit; font-size: 14px; font-family: inherit; vertical-align: baseline; outline: 0px;">*Voters with disabilities have the right to assistance in returning an absentee ballot. The voter&rsquo;s assistant can be anyone who is not the voter&rsquo;s employer, an agent of the employer, a representative of their labor union, or a candidate on the ballot. See 52 U.S.C. &sect; 10508</span></p>
    </div>

